Also VERIFIED: the **US Department of Education (2023)** *Guiding Principles for Creating Safe, Inclusive, Supportive, and Fair School Climates* (March 2023) contains a section headed "Ending the practice of corporal punishment in schools," stating that CP "is ineffective and harmful," and names the Good Behavior Game, trauma-informed practices, SEL, restorative practices and PBIS as more effective alternatives (see B10).

